{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 38,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In those days was Hezekiah sick with a mortal disease. And Isaiah the prophet the son of Amoz came to him, and said to him, Thus saith the LORD, Set thy house in order: for thou shalt die, and not live.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Hezekiah turned his face towards the wall, and prayed to the LORD,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said, Remember now, O LORD, I beseech thee, how I have walked before thee in truth and with a perfect heart, and have done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " good in thy sight. And Hezekiah wept bitterly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came the word of the LORD to Isaiah, saying,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go and say to Hezekiah, Thus saith the LORD, the God of David thy father, I have heard thy prayer, I have seen thy tears: behold, I will add to thy days fifteen years.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I will deliver thee and this city from the hand of the king of Assyria: and I will defend this city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a sign to thee from the LORD, that the LORD will do this thing that he hath spoken;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I will bring again the shadow of the degrees, which hath gone down on the sun-dial of Ahaz ten degrees backward. So the sun returned ten degrees, by which degrees it had gone down.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The writing of Hezekiah king of Judah, when he had been sick, and had recovered from his sickness:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said in the cutting off of my days, I shall go to the gates of the grave: I am deprived of the residue of my years.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I said, I shall not see the LORD, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD, in the land of the living: I shall behold man no more with the inhabitants of the world.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My age hath departed, and is removed from me as a shepherd's tent: I have cut off like a weaver my life: he will cut me off with pining sickness: from day ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to night wilt thou make an end of me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I reckoned till morning, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", as a lion, so will he break all my bones: from day ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to night wilt thou make an end of me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like a crane ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "or",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a swallow, so I chattered: I mourned as a dove: my eyes fail ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with looking",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upward: O LORD, I am oppressed; undertake for me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What shall I say? he hath both spoken to me, and himself hath done ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": I shall go softly all my years in the bitterness of my soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD, by these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " live, and in all these ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the life of my spirit: so wilt thou recover me, and make me to live.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, for peace I had great bitterness: but thou hast in love to my soul ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "delivered it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the pit of corruption: for thou hast cast all my sins behind thy back.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the grave cannot praise thee, death can ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " celebrate thee: they that go down into the pit cannot hope for thy truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The living, the living, he shall praise thee, as I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this day: the father to the children shall make known thy truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was ready",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to save me: therefore we will sing my songs to the stringed instruments all the days of our life in the house of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Isaiah had said, Let them take a lump of figs, and lay ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for a plaster upon the boil, and he will recover.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.38.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.38.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hezekiah also had said, What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sign that I shall go up to the house of the LORD?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
